test/parity/goldens/gleam/
glp_gleam/.parity_run.glp

# 3rtask run evidence (orchestration artifacts, not source)
.specify/3rtask/runs/

# feature 078 T062 / register block 49: receipts are EVIDENCE (FR-002) and are ignored;
# the two manifests are DECLARATIONS (FR-019 adoption, FR-023 expected-checks) and are tracked.
# Before this, plan.md said gitignored, .gitattributes pinned eol=lf (a no-op on ignored files),
# and git check-ignore said neither - three artifacts disagreeing about one path.
.specify/receipts/*
!.specify/receipts/adoption-manifest.json
!.specify/receipts/expected-checks.json

# COOP live mailboxes (operator ruling 2026-07-28): the cross-host channel is
# NEVER tracked - no in-branch commit/push/merge logic for live dialogue.
# Git carries COOP state ONLY as deliberate milestone snapshots under
# docs/coop-milestones/ (the mstack pattern: live state out of git, deliberate
# deterministic exports in - same split as .specify/roadmap-sync/exports).
COOP/

# 061 engine-host snapshot file-fallback store (gitignored per contracts/snapshot-store.md)
.glpsnap/

# Roadmap-sync import manifest — DERIVED mirror of the PGlite catalog, which is the
# authority (FR-018: `roadmap import --rebuild-manifest` regenerates it from the catalog).
# Tracked, it conflicted on every multi-host ship (3+ occurrences) because each host's
# import order differs while the catalog state converges. Fleet was unanimous on the fix;
# engineer ruled it 2026-08-11. The deterministic exports under exports/ stay tracked —
# same live-state-out / deliberate-exports-in split as COOP/ above.
.specify/roadmap-sync/.import-manifest.json

# Same class, same reasoning: per-host DERIVED import bookkeeping regenerated from the
# catalog on every round. Multi-megabyte and divergent per host by construction, so
# tracking them reintroduces exactly the conflict the manifest ruling removed.
.specify/roadmap-sync/.import-provenance/
.specify/roadmap-sync/.import-refused.json

# 064 durable-listener-service-box: operator registration + WAL file fallback
